## Round 5: the legs and the feet color try 2

### The orchestrator decision

Orchestrator decision 2026-11-07, after a look at the contact sheet. The PM rule says a
body-part picture shows a child pointing to the part. In the legs try 1 picture and in the feet
try 1 picture the child stands with both arms hanging. The judge notes read "one hand hangs by
the side with the finger pointing down" for the legs, and "her arms hang down with the fingers
pointing down ... The pointing is a weak action (note only)" for the feet. By the same rule as
the arms row, both tries count as failed tries. Each row gets a color try 2. No other row changes.
The delivery of round 4 is to be rewritten after the judge. The maker wrote no delivery file and
changed no file in the handoff folder in this round.

### The change of the two spec files

Only the picture sentences of the `colorPrompt` and the `goal` of the two spec files changed.
Every other sentence of each prompt stays as it was, including the white-background, the no-text,
and the rated-G sentences. Every other field of both files stays as it was, and the `mustShow`
list of each row stays as it was.

The legs prompt now shows Pat standing with his feet a little apart. He reaches down with both
hands, and the index fingertip of each hand touches the front of his leg on the same side. The
feet prompt now shows Nan sitting on the plain white floor with both legs stretched out toward
the viewer, and the index fingertip of one hand touches the toe of one shoe.

